{"duration": 80.239, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "Galileo aimed a spyglass at Jupiter, then spent his life under house arrest.", "start": 0.08, "end": 4.202}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Galileo saw four moons circling Jupiter.", "start": 4.622, "end": 6.889}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Most educated people still believed Earth stood at the center.", "start": 7.109, "end": 10.467}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Many astronomers refused to believe Galileo could have found them.", "start": 10.687, "end": 13.95}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Other astronomers struggled to confirm his observations.", "start": 14.17, "end": 17.229}, {"beat": 2, "text": "In 1613, Grand Duchess Christina of Florence raised biblical objections to Earth's motion with Galileo's friend Castelli.", "start": 17.649, "end": 25.497}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Galileo wrote that the Bible guides faith, not science.", "start": 25.717, "end": 28.773}, {"beat": 2, "text": "In 1616, Church judges ruled Earth's motion formally heretical.", "start": 28.993, "end": 33.286}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Galileo was ordered never to hold, teach, or defend it.", "start": 33.506, "end": 36.506}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it is like telling a teacher the answer key is wrong.", "start": 36.926, "end": 39.82}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Galileo's telescope turned Earth's motion from opinion into evidence.", "start": 40.24, "end": 44.227}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Jupiter's moons and Venus's phases fit a moving Earth.", "start": 44.447, "end": 47.429}, {"beat": 4, "text": "But Galileo also claimed Scripture could be set aside in astronomy.", "start": 47.649, "end": 51.394}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The Inquisition treated that claim as a second heresy.", "start": 51.614, "end": 54.32}, {"beat": 5, "text": "In 1632, Galileo published a book defending Earth's motion.", "start": 54.74, "end": 58.724}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The book called geocentrists 'simpletons'.", "start": 58.944, "end": 60.923}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Pope Urban VIII banned its sale.", "start": 61.143, "end": 62.887}, {"beat": 5, "text": "In 1633, the Inquisition found Galileo 'vehemently suspect of heresy'.", "start": 63.107, "end": 67.993}, {"beat": 6, "text": "Galileo abjured his views and stayed under house arrest for life.", "start": 68.413, "end": 72.025}, {"beat": 6, "text": "The twist: the famous last words 'And yet it moves' have no evidence.", "start": 72.245, "end": 76.0}, {"beat": 6, "text": "The earliest written account came a century after his death.", "start": 76.22, "end": 79.119}], "words": [{"w": "Galileo", "start": 0.128, "end": 0.728, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "aimed", "start": 0.778, "end": 0.953, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "a", "start": 0.978, "end": 1.003, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "spyglass", "start": 1.078, "end": 1.553, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "at", "start": 1.603, "end": 1.653, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Jupiter,", "start": 1.703, "end": 2.428, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "then", "start": 2.478, "end": 2.603, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "spent", "start": 2.653, "end": 2.828, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "his", "start": 2.853, "end": 2.978, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "life", "start": 3.028, "end": 3.253, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "under", "start": 3.278, "end": 3.453, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "house", "start": 3.503, "end": 3.728, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "arrest.", "start": 3.778, "end": 4.219, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Galileo", "start": 4.691, "end": 5.241, "line": 1, "beat": 1}, {"w": "saw", "start": 5.291, "end": 5.441, "line": 1, "beat": 1}, {"w": "four", "start": 5.541, "end": 5.766, "line": 1, "beat": 1}, {"w": "moons", "start": 5.816, "end": 6.041, "line": 1, "beat": 1}, {"w": "circling", "start": 6.116, "end": 6.441, "line": 1, "beat": 1}, {"w": "Jupiter.", "start": 6.491, "end": 6.99, "line": 1, "beat": 1}, {"w": "Most", "start": 7.175, "end": 7.4, "line": 2, "beat": 1}, {"w": "educated", "start": 7.475, "end": 7.975, "line": 2, "beat": 1}, {"w": "people", "star